Beyond 10K nodes, Neo4j still scales well because graph traversals remain relationship-based. The main optimizations are creating indexes on customerId, accountId, deviceId, and transactionId, enforcing uniqueness constraints, avoiding full graph scans, and retrieving only relevant subgraphs. For very large datasets (100K to millions of nodes), visualization should be customer-centric rather than loading the entire graph, and production deployments should use clustered or AuraDB environments for scalability and availability.

